       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
       PROGRAM-ID. PB174FIEA.
       OPTIONS.
           FLOAT-BINARY DEFAULT IS HIGH-ORDER-RIGHT.
      *> kb/Work PB174 - THE PER-ITEM ENDIANNESS-PHRASE OF THE USAGE
      *> CLAUSE (13.18.60.2 GENERAL FORMAT, VERIFIED AGAINST THE
      *> PRINTED PAGE: "FLOAT-BINARY-32 [ ENDIANNESS-PHRASE ]"), AND
      *> ITS PRECEDENCE OVER THE OPTIONS-SUPPLIED IMPLIED PHRASE.
      *> THE PRECEDENCE IS NOT A PREFERENCE - 11.9.8.3 SR3 IMPLIES THE
      *> CLAUSE'S HIGH-ORDER-RIGHT ONLY FOR AN ITEM "IN WHICH AN
      *> ENDIANNESS-PHRASE IS NOT SPECIFIED", SO AN ITEM THAT WROTE
      *> ONE IS OUTSIDE THE RULE ALTOGETHER. 13.18.60.4 GR19a/b GIVE
      *> THE PHRASES THEIR MEANING: HIGH-ORDER-LEFT = BIG-ENDIAN,
      *> HIGH-ORDER-RIGHT = LITTLE-ENDIAN.
      *>
      *> EXPECTED VALUES ARE COMPUTED FROM THE STANDARD, NOT FROM A
      *> RUN. BINARY32 1.5 = 0x3FC00000 (60559:2020 3.4, GR14):
      *>   B32-L  ITEM SAYS HIGH-ORDER-LEFT  -> BIG    -> 3F C0 00 00
      *>   B32-D  ITEM SAYS NOTHING          -> OPTIONS -> 00 00 C0 3F
      *>   C1     COMP-1, GR13/GR21 IMPLEMENTOR PIN, GR19c SCOPES THE
      *>          CLAUSE TO THE STANDARD USAGES -> BIG -> 3F C0 00 00
      *> A ROUND-TRIP GOLDEN CANNOT SEE BYTE ORDER (BOTH LANES REVERSE
      *> - SELF-INVERSE), SO THE DISCRIMINATING LEG READS SINGLE BYTES
      *> WITH FUNCTION ORD (15.70 - ORDINAL POSITION, NATIVELY BYTE+1):
      *> ORD 0x3F = 64 AND ORD 0x00 = 1.
       DATA DIVISION.
       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
       01 GH.
          05 B32-L USAGE FLOAT-BINARY-32 HIGH-ORDER-LEFT VALUE 1.5.
          05 B32-D USAGE FLOAT-BINARY-32 VALUE 1.5.
          05 C1 USAGE COMP-1 VALUE 1.5.
       01 XH PIC X(12).
       PROCEDURE DIVISION.
       MAIN.
           MOVE GH TO XH
      *> BYTES 1-4: THE ITEM'S OWN HIGH-ORDER-LEFT WINS -> 3F C0 00 00.
           DISPLAY "L=[" FUNCTION ORD(XH(1:1)) " "
               FUNCTION ORD(XH(4:1)) "]"
      *> BYTES 5-8: NO PHRASE -> THE OPTIONS HIGH-ORDER-RIGHT IS
      *> IMPLIED (11.9.8.3 SR3) -> 00 00 C0 3F.
           DISPLAY "D=[" FUNCTION ORD(XH(5:1)) " "
               FUNCTION ORD(XH(8:1)) "]"
      *> BYTES 9-12: COMP-1 IS NOT A STANDARD BINARY FLOAT USAGE
      *> (3.166), SO NEITHER THE CLAUSE NOR A PHRASE REACHES IT.
           DISPLAY "C=[" FUNCTION ORD(XH(9:1)) " "
               FUNCTION ORD(XH(12:1)) "]"
      *> AND THE VALUE LANE IS UNDISTURBED IN BOTH DIRECTIONS.
           DISPLAY "V=[" B32-L " " B32-D " " C1 "]"
           STOP RUN.
